  "abstract": "Add a horizon-wise population-mean alignment penalty: \u03bb_pop \u00b7 mean_t |mean_{B,N}(y_pred[t]) \u2212 mean_{B,N}(y_true[t])| on top of MAE+curvature. Tests whether correcting global bias per horizon helps late steps. Config: p=36, H=128, drop=0.05, lr=9e\u22124, clip=1.0, learn_gamma=False, \u03bb_pop=1e\u22123.",
